    {
      "id": "s1",
      "template": "title",
      "narration": "Typing fires your search fifty times a second. Debounce fixes that.",
      "motion": "popWords",
      "text": {
        "heading": "Stop spamming your API",
        "sub": "debounce, in 40 seconds",
        "kicker": "JavaScript"
      },
      "durationSec": 4.01
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "template": "diagram",
      "narration": "Debounce waits until the events stop. Every keystroke resets a timer, and the function only runs once after a short pause.",
      "motion": "build",
      "text": {
        "heading": "How debounce works",
        "diagram": {
          "accentIndex": 2,
          "loop": "every key resets the timer",
          "boxes": [
            {
              "title": "events",
              "items": [
                "k k k k k"
              ]
            },
            {
              "title": "timer",
              "items": [
                "resets on each key"
              ]
            },
            {
              "title": "runs once",
              "items": [
                "after 300ms of quiet"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "durationSec": 7.648
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "template": "code",
      "narration": "Here's the whole thing. Keep a timer in a closure. Clear it on every call, and set it again. Only the last call survives.",
      "motion": "typewriter",
      "text": {
        "heading": "The implementation",
        "code": [
          "function debounce(fn, delay) {",
          "  let t;",
          "  return (...args) => {",
          "    clearTimeout(t);",
          "    t = setTimeout(() => fn(...args), delay);",
          "  };",
          "}"
        ]
      },
      "durationSec": 7.214
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "template": "bullets",
      "narration": "Use it anywhere events fire too fast: search as you type, window resize, scroll handlers, and auto-save.",
      "motion": "slideUp",
      "text": {
        "heading": "Where to use it",
        "bullets": [
          "search-as-you-type",
          "resize & scroll handlers",
          "auto-save on input"
        ],
        "kicker": "Use cases"
      },
      "durationSec": 6.309
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "template": "bullets",
      "narration": "Quick contrast. Debounce waits for quiet. Throttle runs at most once per interval. Don't mix them up.",
      "motion": "slideUp",
      "text": {
        "heading": "Debounce vs throttle",
        "bullets": [
          "debounce: wait for a pause",
          "throttle: once per interval",
          "pick by the behavior you want"
        ],
        "kicker": "Comparison"
      },
      "durationSec": 6.087
    },
